{
  "format": 4,
  "kind": "session",
  "name": "Shown status and seen",
  "description": "Others see only the shown status, and seen is the time when it last became offline (capability status). A disconnect and a change to a chosen invisible send the same frame: a shown offline with seen. While the shown status stays offline, seen stays: connections that come and go send nothing, a user notification for another field carries neither status nor seen, and a later listing carries the same seen. When the shown status leaves offline, the kept seen is no longer shown, and the next change to offline brings a new one. A dnd user who disconnects is shown offline with seen. A sign-in drops the kept statuses and seen, and the listing sets them again. The user's own status is the chosen status from you: a complete listing object that carries the shown offline and seen does not replace it, and the user's own seen is never shown.",
  "references": [
    "PROTOCOL.md#21-log_id",
    "PROTOCOL.md#331-user-objects",
    "PROTOCOL.md#451-values",
    "PROTOCOL.md#452-delivery",
    "PROTOCOL.md#454-sign-in"
  ],
